Specifications followed
-----------------------

HyperFrames (HTML rendered to video)
  Apache License 2.0. Motion Studio follows its timing contract: timing
  attributes, [start, end) visibility windows, determinism rules, tracks and
  safe zones (ADR 0010). No HyperFrames code is copied or bundled; Diazo's own
  runtime implements the contract with WAAPI and CSS.

EffectCraft (motion effects)
  MIT License OR Apache License 2.0 (dual licensed, at your option).
  Copyright (c) 2026 ArtCraft Team and the EffectCraft contributors.
  Reference: https://github.com/storytold/effectcraft, revision
  0d1fc924a35e09644e0d9f2f2457cce11da94cb0.
  The GLSL effect bodies in src/lib/motion/gl.ts and the registry in
  shared/motionFx.ts are Diazo's own implementations of the standard image
  algorithms (blur taps, luminance ops, hash noise, distance fields).
  EffectCraft's effect modules informed the family and parameter names at
  the revision above. No EffectCraft code is copied or bundled; every
  shader is an original implementation and the effect ids are Diazo's own.

W3C Compositing and Blending Level 1 (element blend modes)
  W3C Document License. Reference: https://www.w3.org/TR/compositing-1/
  The blend-mode math in shared/motionBlend.ts (blendPixel,
  compositePixel, BLEND_GLSL) implements the spec's separable and
  non-separable blend formulas and its premultiplied source-over
  composite. The extended separable modes beyond the spec's list use the
  common published Photoshop-era definitions. All implementations are
  Diazo's own; no external code is copied or bundled.
